{"name":"Lagos","slug":"lagos","region":"Africa","lat":6.52,"lon":3.38,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Lagos has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.5 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 15% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 90% of a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 15 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 6 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 0.5 °C, against 0.1 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb is the dry season in Lagos; rainfall has tended to decline in this record, a trend that station records cannot yet confirm. El Niño has a modest but consistent effect toward a drier season with less intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.5 points per decade, roughly 4 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a modest but consistent effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is substantial. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 0.8 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is likely (about 75% chance), partly because of an uncertain long-term drying trend, and a less humid season than normal is likely (about 75% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":27.4153,"trend_per_decade":0.1937,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.4528,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1346,"enso_p":0.0011,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1378,"intrinsic_sd":0.3156,"effect_this_season":0.2961,"effect_ratio":0.9384,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":6.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7565,"p_below":0.0027,"p_near":0.0166,"p_above":0.9806,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":15.2882,"values":[26.571,27.203,26.714,26.659,26.77,26.484,25.63,26.892,26.691,26.708,26.809,26.79,26.784,27.155,26.291,26.914,26.867,26.555,27.135,27.131,26.649,26.51,27.568,26.661,26.484,26.325,26.619,26.784,27.12,27.105,26.79,27.168,26.674,26.919,26.907,26.749,26.829,27.373,26.319,26.986,27.161,26.865,26.971,27.15,27.248,27.213,27.092,27.755,27.32,27.19,27.269,27.173,27.381,27.575,27.704,27.68,27.492,27.071,27.459,28.286,27.358,27.236,27.747,27.306,27.154,27.351,27.928,27.391,27.91,28.022,27.932,28.003,27.841,28.597,28.324],"forecast_mean":28.1718,"forecast_sd":0.3396,"fit":{"a2027":27.8756,"b":0.1346,"c":0.0194,"tercile_low":27.2288,"tercile_high":27.47},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1452,"trend_p":0.0011,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0509,"enso_p":0.443,"confidence":"