 run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 35% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 1.5 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 20 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this warm would come about once every 23 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 0.5 °C, against 0.3 °C for the coldest days. Mar–May rainfall has fallen by about 5% per decade. El Niño's effect is uncertain, with a slight tilt toward a drier season. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.2 points per decade, roughly 1 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 0.9 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is likely (about 80% chance), mostly because of the long-term trend rather than El Niño. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":27.7939,"trend_per_decade":0.2,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.5001,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1776,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.3454,"intrinsic_sd":0.2292,"effect_this_season":0.3908,"effect_ratio":1.7049,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":23.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.894,"p_below":0.0,"p_near":0.0005,"p_above":0.9995,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":19.539,"values":[26.842,27.12,26.934,26.733,26.737,26.705,26.53,27.188,27.184,26.889,27.21,27.055,27.141,27.569,27.141,27.55,27.18,26.83,27.492,27.441,27.271,27.035,27.641,27.022,26.971,26.789,27.419,26.857,27.409,27.423,27.307,27.251,27.895,27.34,27.285,27.499,27.869,27.734,27.312,27